      "title": "Evidence gathering, Knowledge Graph ingestion, and authoring provenance",
      "description": "Five-step research, scholarly retrieval, Knowledge Graph ingestion, relevancy assessment, and authoring-provenance workflow required of research and authoring agents: decompose topic areas and shortlist needed papers and datasets, query scholarly and data databases (Crossref/DOI, arXiv, PubMed, InspireHEP, OpenAlex, Semantic Scholar, Google Scholar, and reference data registries), ingest into declared KG subgraphs, record relevancy and claim boundaries, and wire authoring provenance notes and formal citations into authored blocks.",
